\section{Evaluation and Results}\label{sec:evaluation}

The evaluation asks how far the fixed-profile design satisfies the four
criteria defined in \Cref{sec:method}: semantic coherence, bounded safety,
targeted fault sensitivity, and constructibility. Following FEDS
\citep{venable2016feds}, the first three criteria are evaluated artificially
with executable schemas, canonical vectors, validators, finite models,
and countermodels. The historical rival comparison is reported separately as
method history. Constructibility is evaluated with a
private historical SF-3 reference path and separately identified RM-2025
precursor cases. These objects have different semantic identities and cannot
upgrade one another's claims.

